From: Custom Kernel Build
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 22:56:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] block: Set none as default I/O scheduler for blk-mq

Make none the default I/O scheduler instead of mq-deadline to improve
startup performance and reduce latency. This allows userspace to select
an appropriate scheduler at runtime.

The change applies to multi-queue block devices, simplifying the default
scheduler selection logic by returning NULL from elevator_get_default(),
which results in the none scheduler being used by default.

Signed-off-by: Kernel Builder <builder@kernel.local>
---
 block/elevator.c | 15 ++++-----------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/block/elevator.c b/block/elevator.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/block/elevator.c
+++ b/block/elevator.c
@@ -556,16 +556,9 @@ static struct elevator_type *elevator_get_default(struct request_queue *q)
 	if (q->tag_set->flags & BLK_MQ_F_NO_SCHED_BY_DEFAULT)
 		return NULL;
 
-	/*
-	 * For single queue devices, default to using mq-deadline. If we have
-	 * multiple queues or mq-deadline is not available, default to "none".
-	 */
-	if (q->nr_hw_queues == 1)
-		return elevator_get(q, "mq-deadline", false);
-	return elevator_get(q, "none", false);
+	/*
+	 * Start with no elevator; userspace can select a scheduler later.
+	 */
+	return NULL;
 }
 
 /*
